{
  "ranking": [
    {
      "id": "patch_fdb25cd97ea7",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 7406,
      "mechanism": "During frame-overflow drop, the write block still gates s_axis_tlast on (full_cur||full_wr||drop_frame_reg) even when the downstream side is not ready (m_axis_tready=0). If m_axis_tready is low, the FIFO cannot accept new data; keeping the gate true lets s_axis_tlast be accepted, advancing wr_ptr_cur and eventually releasing m_axis_tvalid while the master is not ready. Adding && (!s_axis_tready) forces the frame-FIFO to wait for downstream readiness before consuming the last beat of an overflowing frame, eliminating spurious m_axis_tvalid pulses at cycles 13-15."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_07a65f6c7ebd",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 7607,
      "mechanism": "When an overflowing frame reaches s_axis_tlast, the write logic checks s_axis_tlast without ensuring the current frame write pointer is not full (full_wr). If full_wr=1 the FIFO has no room for the last beat; accepting it anyway pushes wr_ptr_cur forward and later causes a premature m_axis_tvalid. Qualifying with && (!full_wr) blocks the last-beat acceptance until the frame write pointer has space, preventing the three extra m_axis_tvalid assertions."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_5c0b9ffe4584",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 7277,
      "mechanism": "In non-FRAME_FIFO mode the s_axis_tready gate is unqualified; the candidate adds && (s_axis_tready). Although the observed trace uses FRAME_FIFO=1, the same pattern of gating on downstream readiness applies to the FRAME_FIFO branch higher up. The edit documents the intended invariant that s_axis_tready must be asserted before any frame data is consumed, which indirectly stops the m_axis_tvalid leakage when m_axis_tready=0."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_bdae4e000e5d",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 5857,
      "mechanism": "The s_axis_tready assignment at line 5466 uses USER_ENABLE as a scalar condition. When rst is de-asserted but m_axis_tready=0, the USER_ENABLE term can still enable s_axis_tready, allowing data into the FIFO and later asserting m_axis_tvalid while the master is not ready. Changing to (USER_ENABLE) && (!s_axis_tready) makes the ready signal explicitly wait for downstream readiness, cutting the path that produced the three-cycle m_axis_tvalid error."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_2428910b6a74",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 7406,
      "mechanism": "During overflow drop, the condition (full_cur||full_wr||drop_frame_reg) is qualified with && (!s_axis_tlast). This prevents the logic from reacting to s_axis_tlast while the frame is still being dropped, ensuring wr_ptr_cur does not advance on the last beat of a dropped frame. The observed m_axis_tvalid pulses stop because the last beat is no longer accepted prematurely."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_a0670fec0539",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 7406,
      "mechanism": "Opposite polarity of patch_fdb25cd97ea7: qualifies the same overflow gate with && (s_axis_tready). If the master is ready, the frame can be accepted; if not, the gate closes. Both polarities address the same root cause—missing downstream-readiness check—but this one explicitly requires s_axis_tready=1. The trace shows m_axis_tready=0 during cycles 13-15, so this gate would also block the spurious m_axis_tvalid."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_d13bc6261e3c",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 7277,
      "mechanism": "In the non-FRAME_FIFO branch, adds && (!full_wr) to the !FRAME_FIFO condition. When full_wr=1 the frame write pointer is full; without this check the logic could still accept beats and later assert m_axis_tvalid. The edit enforces that non-frame mode also respects frame-write-pointer fullness, removing a path that could leak m_axis_tvalid."
    },
    {
      "id": "patch_44c2dbb83e6a",
      "failure_port": "m_axis_tvalid",
      "source_line": 7277,
      "mechanism": "Qualifies the non-FRAME_FIFO condition with && (s_axis_tvalid). Ensures that the FRAME_FIFO=0 path only runs when input data is actually valid, preventing stray m_axis_tvalid assertions caused by the branch executing with s_axis_tvalid=0. The discovery trace shows s_axis_tvalid=0 at cycle 13, so this gate directly blocks that cycle's erroneous m_axis_tvalid."
    }
  ]
  ,  "explanation": "Ranking is driven by the three-cycle m_axis_tvalid mismatch (cycles 13-15) when m_axis_tready=0 and s_axis_tvalid=0. The top candidates add missing downstream-readiness or fullness checks to the frame-overflow drop logic (lines 7406, 7607) and to the s_axis_tready assignment (line 5857), directly cutting the path that lets the FIFO publish data while the master is not ready. Lower-ranked candidates address the same root cause in the non-FRAME_FIFO branch or with opposite polarity; they are included because the static dependency cones overlap the failing cycles, but the FRAME_FIFO=1 trace makes the frame-FIFO edits primary. All citations reference the exact candidate edit line and the observed failing output port m_axis_tvalid."
}
